 "literal": "Great valor, they say, is fearlessness; when one (hardship) has befallen (a foe), benevolence is further its sharp edge.",
 "translation": "They say great valor is fearlessness in battle. But showing benevolence to a fallen foe is the sharp edge of that valor.",
